Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ci.yml, web-build.yml: paths-ignore/paths filters + timeout-minutes on
  every job so an unrelated change (docs-only, api-only) doesn't spin up
  a full monorepo npm ci + build it doesn't need. Repo is public so
  Actions minutes are unlimited — this is about fast feedback and not
  hogging the org's shared concurrent-job slots, not a per-minute bill.
- web-build.yml: added the concurrency group it was missing (ci.yml and
  e2e.yml already had one), so repeated pushes to a PR don't pile up
  parallel redundant builds.
- presubmit.yml: pinned presubmit/ai-reviewer to its v0.2.5 commit SHA
  instead of the movable tag — this action runs with
  pull-requests:write/issues:write on pull_request_target.
- deploy-ec2.yml (new): CD workflow for the AWS free-tier EC2 box from
  docs/AWS_FREE_TIER_RUNBOOK.md. Authenticates via GitHub OIDC (zero
  stored AWS credentials) into a least-privilege role, then pushes the
  redeploy through SSM Send-Command (git pull + docker compose up) —
  no SSH key, no long-lived access key in repo secrets. Runs after CI
  goes green on main, or manually via workflow_dispatch.
- docs/deployment/GITHUB_ACTIONS_OIDC_SETUP.md (new): one-time AWS
  console steps (OIDC provider, IAM role + trust policy, repo variables)
  required before deploy-ec2.yml can run.

Left e2e.yml untouched (explicit review-only stub, if: false, not yet
wired to real infra) and kept the CI test job non-blocking, per request.
